    "id" : 7,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.672, 492.766, 485.329, 538.594 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Embedded toric resolutions of ADE-singularities were studied in [18, 19]. Here differently we construct regular refinements of Gr¨bner fans of each members of them. This leads us their embedded toric resolutions [1, 2]. Additionally, these resolutions will be minimal which means that:"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 8,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.672, 476.621, 410.656, 486.584 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Definition 4.2. An embedded toric resolution is called minimal if"
  }, {
    "type" : "list",
    "pdfua_tag" : "L",
    "id" : 9,
    "level" : "3",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 138.627, 445.638, 485.327, 474.629 ],
